# LIMIT — HSSS Source/Structure Record

## 1. Source
`limit.c` is the authoritative implementation. It uses standard C11 facilities plus native POSIX/Windows APIs selected by platform macros.

## 2. Specification
The executable is a read-only inventory tool. It identifies ELF, PE, and Mach-O binaries, reports file size and available filesystem time information, and emits a stable key/value record. `MEARVK-META` is an executable-build metadata contract; it does not replace OS-native executable metadata.

## 3. System Boundary
Input: local directory path. Output: stdout records. Errors: stderr and non-zero status. No executable is launched by `limit`.

## 4. Compiler Relationship
`build.sh` searches for the locally built GCC 16.2.0 compiler in the repository before using the system compiler. When `-fme-metadata` is available it passes explicit edition, version, company, and source values to the compiler.

## 5. Authority
Compiler metadata describes build provenance. It does not establish legal ownership, fiduciary status, or execution permission. Such values must be explicitly supplied and independently interpreted.

## 6. Verification
Build with `./build.sh`; verify with `./limit --version`; inspect a directory with `./limit PATH`. If the derived GCC has not been built, the script reports that it is falling back to the system compiler.
